  "topic": "Meta (Muse Image)",
  "context": "Meta has released **Muse Image**, its first proprietary AI image-generation model from Meta Superintelligence Labs, as part of the new Muse family that is replacing the earlier Llama models.[1][2][4] Muse Image is tightly integrated with the **Muse Spark** large language model, enabling so-called *agentic* behavior where the system can reason through prompts, search the web, and plan before generating images, and it is natively built to interpret complex, conversational instructions, blend multiple photos, and even produce legible styled text and functional QR codes within images.[2][3][6] The model is already embedded in the Meta AI app and website, Instagram, and WhatsApp, with planned expansion to Facebook and Messenger, and supports creative tools like transforming user photos, redesigning rooms, drawing directly on images, and mentioning Instagram accounts so their likeness can be incorporated into AI-generated photos.[2][3][4]\n\nTh
